# Oracle: VD cir-subckt (a value that folds to a constant at parse time is a default an instance
# may override; one that reads a parameter is dependent); DIALECT-VACASK Appendix A runs c1
# (`2*3`, `M_PI`, `sqrt(4)` overridable, `q*2` not), t2. Formals go to the head in order; the
# dependent entries stay in the body as local parameters. VD cir-subckt-nested (nesting).
# codes:
file "subckt_params.sim" deck
  title "formals and locals"
  param q = 5
  subckt s (a b) x=(2 * 3) y=3.141592653589793 z=(sqrt(4)) u=7
    param w = q * 2
    param v = x + 1
    subckt inner (c) k=1
